      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im working in a jupyter notebook and im getting this annoying SettingWithCopyWarning when i try to add a new column to a dataframe that i sliced from a bigger one. can u tell me why this happens and how i can fix it properly?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The `SettingWithCopyWarning` pops up because pandas is unsure if you are modifying a view of the original DataFrame or a completely new copy. It's a warning, not usually an error, but it means your changes might not stick where you expect them to. To fix this, you should explicitly create a copy of the slice you are working with, like this: `df_new = df_original[condition].copy()`. This tells pandas definitively that you are starting a new, independent DataFrame, preventing the ambiguity.",
      "source": "target",
